  "description": "Set five cones in two staggered rows: three near the boards and two toward the middle, spread from the face-off circle to just before the blue line. Skaters line up in the corner. One at a time, wrap around each cone in turn, like a worm wiggling down the ice. After the last cone, the coach passes a puck; skate in and shoot. The next skater goes when the one ahead reaches the third cone.",
